            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0259" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg141"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">314.115C43/136: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-07-12T17:00:00-06:00">July 12, 1929—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:02 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>91. Referring to Department’s telegram of July 10, 3 p.m. The Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs has told me that he will study my memorandum of today<anchor
                        n="26" xml:id="d147-f1"/> regarding Shufeldt and submit the matter to the
                    Cabinet on the 16th.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
